transcript ever saw a bug or a task at a gate. `pipeline-runner` writes the same block, so `/sprint`'s queue and the cockpit show each sprint gate's real options.\n- **Answer from the cockpit** (`adlc-flightdeck` 0.6.0–0.8.1). The flightdeck draws in the band above the prompt; at an open gate its GATE block lists the options with their consequences, the recommended one first. Pressing one — letters `a b d e f g i j` once the band has focus, never digits — sends it as your own message; an option with an argument (`fix <ids>`) takes it in an input. At implement and review the reply carries `[flightdeck] viewed 4/7 files` in plain sight; `trail gate` lifts it into the round (`viewed`, `via pane`) and keeps the note to your words. The mod's dialog branch is deleted; it answers no tool call.\n- **The band is the cockpit** (0.7.0–0.8.0): no pane; one row, *open* or *max*; the REQs in flight as a strip, the one at a gate first; below the narrow breakpoint the phase tabs become a list. Plan vs actual diffs the REQ's own branch (`pipeline-state.json` → `branch`) against its merge-base; with another branch checked out it is committed-only and says so.\n- **Compact at the gate, on your say-so.** *compact first* on the GATE block compacts with instructions built from the REQ's state, then sends; Settings → *compact mode* `button | suggest | never`. The trail hook counts compactions per round (`SessionStart`, `source: compact`). After any compaction `/proceed` re-reads the phase skill, GATE-PROTOCOL, the state and the marker before acting — a skill comes back cut at about 5,000 tokens — and the knowledge hook's snapshot names those files by absolute path, preferring the REQ at a gate.\n- **The trail hook follows the card.** `Stop` takes the REQ from the card's `GATE n/m · … · <ID>` header (two REQs in one checkout land right), copies the marker's options into the round (`ask`), and ignores an `ASK ·` turn. `trail gate --note` takes the reply verbatim: the trailer is lifted out before the 200-character cut (a long reply lost it before), and a note that is only the option is dropped. A vault-relative `--req <REQ_PATH>` resolves exactly.\n- **IDs by their full name** in the mod: `REQ-sf-033` is no longer shown as `REQ-035 · not in this vault`, and `L-REQ-035-1` is not `REQ-035`. The trail hook and vault generator side is the *prefixed IDs* fix below.\n- **`/recover` reads the marker.** `.awaiting-approval` is the gate signal; a stale `gateState` is restored from it (`in-sync-at-gate`), and a marker that disagrees with `currentPhaseGate` is `divergent`.\n- **Predict and summary end the turn too** (`/architect` preflight 5, `/wrapup` 7b): `ASK · Predict` / `ASK · Summary`, reply or `skip`, no marker, not asked again once recorded; the summary is asked before the ship gate's state and marker are written. A proposed ADR's accept/reject folds into the architect gate's options (`approve` · `approve, reject ADR-NNN`) — one gate, no second question.\n- **`trail stats`** (1.12.2) and `/status` 4b gain two lines: *via pane* — gate answers sent from the cockpit against typed ones, rounds recorded before 1.12 counted apart, never as typed — and *compaction* — compactions at gates per round, plus any that fell between gates. A record's `## Trail` carries `· via pane` / `· typed` and `· N compactions` after each decision, so finished work counts too; `--all` gains `via p/t` and `cmp`; `--json` has `via` and `compactions`.\n- `core/manifest.json` → 1.12.0. Patch scripts: `apply-1.12.1.py` (1.12.1 and 1.12.2; idempotent, line endings preserved per file); the mod: `apply-1.12.0.py`, `apply-0.8.1.py`. Mod tests: 87, unchanged by the toolkit tranches.\n- **Deliberately not changed:** `/autopilot` and the decision-maker; the runner's pause-at-the-marker protocol and `/sprint`'s queue replies (both now carry the marker's options); gate semantics; the card's format; no new hook wiring, agent, gate or skill.\n- **On update:** update the mod with the toolkit (`/plug